    "narrative": "For the June 30th slate, the **Austin Waves** offense is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Kyle Tucker** (76.93), both of whom present as elite daily plays. **Gunnar Henderson** occupies the top spot in our rankings, benefiting from a highly favorable matchup against Fedde; the combination of a significant park factor (+16%) and an elite SP xERA of 5.20 provides the highest ceiling on the board. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** remains a must-start despite facing the left-handed Springs, as his high base projection and park-adjusted scoring keep his efficiency well within the elite tier. We are also leaning heavily into **Andy Pages** (72.17) and **Miguel Vargas** (66.77); **Andy Pages** enjoys a stellar +18% boost from park and pitcher skill factors, while **Miguel Vargas** maintains a strong scoring profile due to his spot in the #2 hole and a favorable xwOBA metric against Gibson.\n\nThe decision to solidify the starting nine involved a razor-thin margin regarding our fringe assets. **Curtis Mead** (39.15) was the most difficult exclusion, ultimately failing to clear our strict 40.0 floor for the daily starting rotation. While his park and platoon metrics were competitive, the optimizer prioritized the higher-upside profiles of **Nasim Nunez** (45.92) and **Josh Lowe** (47.10), specifically valuing the speed-related advantages that **Nasim Nunez** brings to our scarce stolen base category. We continue to monitor the status of **Nolan Schanuel** and **Josh Lowe**, as both are currently slotted into projected lineups; should these configurations shift significantly after official posting, we are prepared to pivot to high-floor alternatives. Risks remain regarding the potential for dampened output from our outfielders facing the left-handed tandem of Boyd and Springs, but we remain confident that our core, including the high-upside **Heliot Ramos** (57.03), will provide the necessary efficiency to maintain our rotisserie standing.",
